# DOCKER-USER rules for the Dokploy VM. Not installed anywhere yet.
# Append this whole block (its own *filter ... COMMIT section) to the end of
# /etc/ufw/after.rules and /etc/ufw/after6.rules, then `sudo ufw reload` and check with
# `sudo iptables -S DOCKER-USER` and `sudo ip6tables -S DOCKER-USER`.
#
# Forwarded traffic to Docker/Swarm-published ports (Traefik 80/443, dashboard 3000)
# is accepted only from Tailscale, loopback, and Docker's own bridges. Everything
# else (LAN, WAN, IPv6) goes through `ufw route` rules and is then dropped.
# Based on the homelab's caddy/ufw-docker.rules (host only, never installed there),
# with docker_gwbridge added for Swarm services.
*filter
:DOCKER-USER - [0:0]
:ufw-user-forward - [0:0]
-A DOCKER-USER -m conntrack --ctstate RELATED,ESTABLISHED -j RETURN
-A DOCKER-USER -i lo -j RETURN
-A DOCKER-USER -i tailscale0 -j RETURN
-A DOCKER-USER -i docker0 -j RETURN
-A DOCKER-USER -i docker_gwbridge -j RETURN
-A DOCKER-USER -i br+ -j RETURN
-A DOCKER-USER -j ufw-user-forward
-A DOCKER-USER -j DROP
COMMIT
